{
  "dom_id": "question-324461",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "The price of a deli sandwich is normally distributed with a mean of $\\mu $ dollars and a standard deviation of $$1.10.$ In addition, in $90%$ of cases the price is between $$0.80\\mu $ and $$1.20\\mu .$ Find the average price, **rounding your answer to two decimal places**.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.75\\,$ | $\\,0.80\\,$ | $\\,0.85\\,$ | $\\,0.90\\,$ | $\\,0.95\\,$ | $\\,0.97\\,$ | $\\,0.99\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ |\n\n$\\mu ≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$dollars$",
